WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.800 line:56% position:50% align:center size:90%
“Say” versus “tell”. Quick English rule:
what’s the difference between “say” and “tell”?

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:13.200 line:56% position:50% align:center size:90%
With “say”, we usually focus on the words.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:17.100 line:56% position:50% align:center size:90%
He said, “I’m tired.”

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:21.700 line:56% position:50% align:center size:90%
With “tell”, we usually say who receives the information.

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:26.600 line:56% position:50% align:center size:90%
He told me he was tired. So: say something, but tell someone.

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:27.500 line:56% position:50% align:center size:90%
Remember this: say words, tell a person.
